WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.402
Welcome to our training tips to reduce A to Z guarantee claims and returns.

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:06.560
Customers can file

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.488
an A to Z guarantee claim to ask Amazon to investigate an order or product issue when the seller

00:00:12.488 --> 00:00:12.800
hasn't

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.880
resolved the issue within 48 hours.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.040
You can access this information by searching for the Amazon's A to

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.202
Z guarantee claims help page in Seller Central.

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:25.760
Most customers don't need to resort to the claims

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:26.504
process, however.

00:00:26.504 --> 00:00:32.080
In this training, we'll share tips to help you prevent A to Z guarantee claims

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.025
and returns in the first place.

00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:38.240
A customer might submit a claim or request a return if the product

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.009
they receive doesn't meet their expectations.

00:00:41.009 --> 00:00:44.240
Accurate product detail pages help customers make

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.846
informed buying decisions.

00:00:45.846 --> 00:00:51.200
We recommend you describe your products accurately, use clear images,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.772
and check that your products are matched to the correct ASINs.

00:00:54.772 --> 00:00:56.720
In some instances, you might need

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.461
to cancel a customer's order.

00:00:58.461 --> 00:01:02.640
For example, the customer may have placed an order for a product

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.180
that's out of stock.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:08.800
To maintain the customer's trust, promptly cancel any out of stock orders

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.650
and contact them with an explanation as soon as possible.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.960
Then proactively aim to only list

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.394
available products that you can fulfill.

00:01:17.394 --> 00:01:20.640
Providing excellent customer service can also help reduce

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.180
claims and return requests.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.800
A customer might submit a claim or request a return if they've

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.907
messaged you and haven't received a response within 48 hours.

00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:32.960
They're required to contact you

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.720
before raising a claim, so regularly check your buyer seller messages and respond to customers

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:39.137
promptly.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:44.560
The buyer seller messaging service is your only approved method for communicating with

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.351
Amazon customers.

00:01:45.351 --> 00:01:51.280
You can use this tool to respond to messages directly in Seller Central or your

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.555
registered email's inbox.

00:01:52.555 --> 00:01:58.080
To access the messages page, select the envelope icon in the top right

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.740
corner of the Seller Central home page.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.160
You'll use buyer seller messaging to respond to product

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.652
questions or order delivery issues.

00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:10.640
For order returns or related questions, customers must

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.615
instead contact you through a return request.

00:02:13.615 --> 00:02:17.440
If a customer mistakenly contacts you about a return

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:23.520
through buyer seller messaging, instruct them to raise a request using the online return center.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.695
To respond to a return request, select the main menu icon.

00:02:28.695 --> 00:02:30.720
Hover over orders and select

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.398
Manage Returns.

00:02:31.398 --> 00:02:36.480
A customer might submit a claim if they've sent you a return request and haven't

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.872
received a response.

00:02:37.872 --> 00:02:43.440
Respond to return requests within 48 hours by either approving the request

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.800
or closing it based on the order's return eligibility.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.160
Only close a return request if the order is

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:56.400
ineligible for a return and note that the claim will be granted if you incorrectly close an eligible

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:56.762
one.

00:02:56.762 --> 00:03:03.280
If you close a claim for an ineligible order, always let the customer know why their order was

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:03.685
ineligible.

00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:09.360
If you approve a return request, provide clear guidelines on how the customer can

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.695
return the product.

00:03:10.695 --> 00:03:16.480
Your instructions must include a local return address or a prepaid return label.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:22.000
For instances where you don't want the product back, refund the customer and let them know they

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.689
don't need to return it.

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:28.080
If you'd like to update your return settings, select the gear icon in

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.425
the top right corner of Seller Central and select Return Settings.

00:03:32.425 --> 00:03:34.400
Fulfill your orders with care

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.717
using adequate packaging and trackable shipping methods.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.560
Tracked shipments allow customers to see

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.795
the status of their delivery without needing to contact you first.

00:03:44.795 --> 00:03:46.720
We recommend you also add

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:53.040
insurance or request a signature for high-value orders based on your business judgment or when

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.416
Amazon requests it.

00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:59.920
The valid tracking rate or VTR metric represents the total percentage of

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.560
packages with a valid tracking number during a given 30-day period.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.880
You'll need to maintain a VTR

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:13.360
of at least 95% on eligible orders you fulfill yourself to continue self-fulfilling orders

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.130
without restrictions.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:19.520
To help meet this target, provide the name of the carrier, type of delivery

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.590
service you're using and tracking ID when you confirm a shipment.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.440
Follow these steps to confirm

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.275
or edit tracking information.

00:04:27.275 --> 00:04:29.568
Select the main menu icon.

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:32.320
Hover over orders and choose Manage

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:32.729
Orders.

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:38.461
Enter the order ID into the search field and provide the revised tracking number.

00:04:38.461 --> 00:04:39.280
If you'd

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.600
like to monitor your VTR and other shipping performance metrics, select the main menu icon,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.640
hover over Performance and choose Account Health.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.680
Review the shipping performance section of the

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.720
Account Health page.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.920
One way to help earn customers trust and reduce claims is to follow through on

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.024
your timing commitments.

00:04:59.024 --> 00:05:03.440
In other words, confirm order shipments before the ship by date and

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.472
ensure delivery is completed before the estimated delivery date.

00:05:07.472 --> 00:05:10.160
If a customer's delivery is delayed

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.560
for any reason, notify them through buyer seller messaging and verify that they agree to accept

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.800
a late delivery.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:24.000
As a reminder, an order is considered shipped when the courier first scans the package,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.456
not when the order's shipping label is printed.

00:05:27.456 --> 00:05:30.480
Finally, we recommend using buy shipping services

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.811
or buy shipping for order delivery.

00:05:32.811 --> 00:05:35.920
With buy shipping, you can purchase shipping labels

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.848
individually or in bulk and ship, confirm and track outgoing orders.

00:05:40.848 --> 00:05:42.640
Because these orders are

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:48.480
delivered using a trusted network of shipping carriers, you're protected against A to Z guarantee

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:54.382
claims if the claims are related to delivery issues and you ship the orders on time.

00:05:54.382 --> 00:05:55.120
To access

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:01.630
buy shipping, select the main menu icon, hover over orders and choose Manage Orders.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.560
Find the

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:08.017
order you want to ship and select the buy shipping button that appears next to it.

00:06:08.017 --> 00:06:09.040
Search Use Buy

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:15.072
Shipping Services in Seller Central to learn more about buy shipping and availability.

00:06:15.072 --> 00:06:16.000
Buy shipping

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.554
also helps ensure customers can return their orders without delay.

00:06:20.554 --> 00:06:21.920
In certain marketplaces,

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:27.760
we'll authorize returns that align with Amazon's return policy and provide customers with prepaid

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.430
return shipping labels on your behalf.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:34.880
You can use SAFE-T claims, also known as seller assurance

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:40.560
for e-commerce transactions claims, to appeal our decision to issue a refund to a customer.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.680
To qualify for a SAFE-T claim, we must have already fully refunded the customer.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.960
To review a list of possible reasons you may be eligible for reimbursement,

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.800
search for reimbursement policy for prepaid return labels in Seller Central.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.120
If you'd like

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:04.240
to file a SAFE-T claim, select the main menu icon, hover over orders and choose Manage SAFE-T

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:04.711
Claims.

00:07:04.711 --> 00:07:07.538
Select File a New SAFE-T Claim.

00:07:07.538 --> 00:07:12.720
Enter the order ID for the return and click Check Eligibility.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:18.240
If the order is eligible, we'll ask you to select the reason that best describes the case for your

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.686
reimbursement claim and to attach supporting documentation.

00:07:21.686 --> 00:07:24.640
For example, you might attach proof

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:29.573
that we initiated a return for an item that was outside of the return window.

00:07:29.573 --> 00:07:30.560
After you submit

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.711
the SAFE-T claim, we'll email you to let you know if we've received it.

00:07:34.711 --> 00:07:35.600
Aside from this

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:41.760
notification, any discussion regarding the claim will take place on the Manage SAFE-T Claims page.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:48.160
You now have the tools to help minimize claims and returns and provide a great experience to

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.425
your customers.

00:07:49.425 --> 00:07:53.700
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
